Verdict: PASS. It's written to session_plan/eval_task_2.md and every Checked line is PASS. I didn't run the binary or re-run the suite; the verdict comes from the diff and from reading yoagent 0.25.15's source.

• Task done: before this change, a -p run whose event stream closed before the run's end event (AgentEnd) exited 0, the same as a finished reply. Now it exits 1, prints a one-line "reply cut off" note on stderr, and --output-format json reports is_error: true. Both single-shot paths in main.rs use the same exit-code function as other failed runs, so exit 1 follows the existing convention.
• No false positives on normal runs: yoagent sends AgentEnd on every ending it reaches itself: normal finish, error, rejected input, and Ctrl+C (yoyo's abort only cancels, so the end event still arrives). Ctrl+C and the other signal handlers in yoyo's event loop leave the loop before the new check runs. So only an agent task that actually died sets the new flag.
• Tests and docs: the new tests cover the cut both mid-reply and between messages, with the pipe filter on and off. They also check that completed, retried-then-completed and errored runs aren't flagged, and that stdout is unchanged when AgentEnd arrives. docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md and ARCHITECTURE.md are updated, and no user-facing text says "tracked in #1016".
• Not end to end: the commit says plainly that this was measured at the gate layer, not end to end. A stub that drops the connection goes down yoagent's provider-error and retry path instead, which is a different ending. Reaching this one needs the agent task itself to die.

The flag is set once and never reset, but the interactive REPL never reads it, so this doesn't matter today.
